<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    {%- comment -%}
      Safari tints the notch/status-bar with theme-color. Olive, because the
      page opens on a scrimmed video rather than the bone ground.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#4c4b3b">
    <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">

    {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
      <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 32, height: 32 }}">
    {%- endif -%}

    <title>{{ shop.name }}</title>

    {%- comment -%}
      A password page has no page_description, so this tag was shipping empty —
      which Lighthouse scores as "document does not have a meta description",
      and which is the only text a search result or a shared link has to go on.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign meta_description = page_description
      if meta_description == blank
        assign meta_description = shop.description
      endif
      if meta_description == blank
        assign meta_description = 'Technical gravel apparel, designed in Australia. Join the waitlist for the first run of Bush Riding Shorts.'
      endif
    -%}
    <meta name="description" content="{{ meta_description | escape }}">

    {% render 'meta-tags' %}

    {{ content_for_header }}

    {%- comment -%}
      The same two faces the storefront loads, and the storefront's own tokens.
      This page used to load Instrument Serif and General Sans and hardcode a
      palette of its own, which is how it was still showing the study's yellow
      long after the brand board retired it. Linking alpine.css means the
      palette can only ever be the one the rest of the site is using.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Only the three faces this page actually sets: Inter 400 for body and the
      field, Inter 600 for the chip and the tagline, Archivo 600 for the
      heading. The storefront's nine-weight request belongs on the storefront —
      here it was six font files nobody rendered, in front of first paint.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@600&family=Inter:wght@400;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    {{ 'alpine.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  </head>

  <body class="waitlist">
    <main id="MainContent">
      {{ content_for_layout }}
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
